hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1379","Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sadaqah, narrated to us, Sufyan, who is the son of Husayn, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: The sun went down during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose. He said the salaam during prayer, then he recited a recitation aloud, then he bowed in the manner of what he recited, then he raised his head and recited a similar recitation, then he bowed. As he recited, then he raised his head and prostrated, then he stood up in the second rak’ah, and he did the same as he did in the first rak’ah, then he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon “Two of the signs of God are not diminished by the death of a human being, so if that happens, then prepare for prayer.” He said: That is because Abraham died on that day. Then the people said: This was only for the death of Abraham."
